        ['Hold the base of the mat while combing', 'Pinching the skin-side base of the mat between two fingers while combing the fur out reduces how much the comb tugs on the skin itself.'],
        ['Work from the outer edge of the mat inward', 'Starting at the furthest edge and working toward the skin is gentler than attacking the center first.'],
        ['Reward with treats and keep sessions short', 'A few minutes at a time with breaks and treats keeps a cat more cooperative than one long forced session.'],
        ['Check paw pads and the belly, not just the back', 'Mats often form in overlooked spots like between toes and on the belly, especially in cats that are overweight or have trouble reaching to groom.'],
